From: gpu-nvidia-fix <https://github.com/wintermoot/gpu-nvidia-fix>
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] nvidia: replace removed strncpy() in os_get_current_process_name

Kernel 7.2 removed strncpy() from the kernel API. The destination here
holds a NUL-terminated task name, so strscpy() with the full buffer
length preserves the semantics (the old code copied len-1 bytes and
forced the last byte to NUL; strscpy() always NUL-terminates).

Applies to nvidia-580.173.02.

--- a/nvidia/os-interface.c
+++ b/nvidia/os-interface.c
@@ -730,6 +730,6 @@ void NV_API_CALL os_get_current_process_name(char *buf, NvU32 len)
 {
     task_lock(current);
-    strncpy(buf, current->comm, len - 1);
-    buf[len - 1] = '\0';
+    strscpy(buf, current->comm, len);
+
     task_unlock(current);
 }
